LAB ONLY, never in a package: RB_XLATE_DELAY_US=N spins N microseconds after every
TCG translation (report quadra-m68k-2026-10-24.md, section 2.4). It widens the
window in which the Quadra ROM's delay-loop calibration can take its timer-2
interrupt, so the failure the t2-hold patch prevents shows up in a few dozen
starts: apply after the m68k series (it needs retroboot-q800-t2-hold.patch's
cpu_translation_begin/end), build in a separate tree, run rbd_quadra_hunt.sh with
the variable set, with and without -global mos6522-q800-via1.t2-hold=off.

diff --git a/accel/tcg/translate-all.c b/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
index 2bb08fcfb9..645b943c60 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
@@ -275,6 +275,20 @@ TranslationBlock *tb_gen_code(CPUState *cpu, TCGTBCPUState s)
      */
     cpu_translation_begin();
     tb = tb_gen_code_body(cpu, s);
+    {
+        /* LAB ONLY (not in any package): RB_XLATE_DELAY_US slows every translation */
+        static int64_t rb_delay_ns = -1;
+        if (rb_delay_ns < 0) {
+            const char *e = getenv("RB_XLATE_DELAY_US");
+            rb_delay_ns = e ? atoll(e) * 1000 : 0;
+        }
+        if (rb_delay_ns) {
+            int64_t until = get_clock() + rb_delay_ns;
+            while (get_clock() < until) {
+                /* spin */
+            }
+        }
+    }
     cpu_translation_end();
     return tb;
 #else
